    <ProcessingCommand>
        <Command xmlns="">hifv_flagdata</Command>
        <ParameterSet>
            <Parameter>
                <Keyword xmlns="">hm_tbuff</Keyword>
                <Value xmlns="">1.5int</Value>
            </Parameter>
            <Parameter>
                <Keyword xmlns="">fracspw</Keyword>
                <Value xmlns="">0.01</Value>
            </Parameter>
            <Parameter>
                <Keyword xmlns="">intents</Keyword>
                <Value xmlns="">*POINTING*,*FOCUS*,*ATMOSPHERE*,*SIDEBAND_RATIO*, *UNKNOWN*, *SYSTEM_CONFIGURATION*, *UNSPECIFIED#UNSPECIFIED*</Value>
            </Parameter>
            <!-- Added vs. stock procedure_hifv.xml: TLOW0001's calibrator scans
                 (field 1: BP/phase/delay, field 3: flux) come out of the
                 stock recipe 100% flagged (reduction weblog stage3, job
                 2315), which starves hifv_testBPdcals of data and crashes
                 it. VERIFIED by fast-check (isolated single-scan tests, see
                 reduction/_fastcheck and reduction/_subreftest):
                   template, quack : confirmed near-zero effect on their own;
                                     turning them off alone does NOT fix the
                                     100% flagging (tested, still ~100%).
                   online (ANOS+subreflector) : ANOS alone flags ~19% of the
                                     scans it touches (real "not on source"
                                     settle time); subreflector alone is ~0%
                                     except full-scan hits on 2 scans (real
                                     hardware fault window on ea14/ea08).
                                     Neither dominates alone; the ~100% is a
                                     pile-up of several small, real, mostly
                                     independent problems (ANOS + subreflector
                                     + shadowing + scattered zero-valued
                                     cells on ea14/ea12/ea08) each touching
                                     different antennas at different moments
                                     of the same short scan, compounding via
                                     baseline-count non-linearity. Raw DATA
                                     is confirmed NOT mostly zero anywhere
                                     (Bandpass/Flux/Target all ~3.9% zero
                                     cells), so there is real usable signal
                                     under most of this flagging.
                 See fastcheck2 (online=False, template=False, quack=False)
                 for whether relaxing online recovers usable data; update
                 this file's online parameter based on that result before
                 trusting a full run built on it, and re-check the stage3
                 weblog's flagged-data-summary table afterwards regardless. -->
            <Parameter>
                <Keyword xmlns="">template</Keyword>
                <Value xmlns="">False</Value>
            </Parameter>
            <Parameter>
                <Keyword xmlns="">quack</Keyword>
                <Value xmlns="">False</Value>
            </Parameter>
        </ParameterSet>
    </ProcessingCommand>

